    "result_text": "The Soundex implementation matches all standard reference values (including the tricky H/W transparency and vowel-separator cases). The change is complete and the full test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI redesigned the owner identity key and duplicate detection to match the specification.\n\n**New identity key** (`OwnerIdentity.java`): `identityKey` is now the lower-case hex **SHA-256** of `normalizedTelephone + '|' + lowerEmail + '|' + soundex(lastName)` \u2014 a 64-char hex string, replacing the old plaintext `telephone|email|householdId`.\n\n**New Soundex utility** (`Soundex.java`): a self-contained, standard American Soundex implementation (no new dependency), verified against known reference values.\n\n**Hard-duplicate 409** (`EnsureUniqueIdentity.java`): unchanged in mechanism \u2014 it already routes through `OwnerIdentity.key`, so it now compares the new key. It still ignores soft-deleted owners, and the email-domain blocklist still runs first (in `BuildOwner` via `OwnerEmails`). The separate householdId-based 409 is gone because the key no longer contains householdId \u2014 so two owners with the same last name/postcode but different telephones now get distinct keys and are **not** rejected.\n\n**Soft-match** (`AssignPossibleDuplicate.java`): rewritten to trigger when the `identityKey` **differs** but `soundex(lastName)` **and** postcode match (ignoring deleted owners, lowest-id wins). So the same-name/same-postcode/different-telephone case now becomes a soft match instead of a 409.\n\n**Kept**: `AssignHousehold`/`Households` still compute `householdId` (now only for household-size/membership derivations, not duplicate detection), and the `sharesHousehold` bypass behavior.\n\n**Docs**: updated the `owners.POST.yml` pipeline comments, `openapi.yml` descriptions/example for `identityKey`/`possibleDuplicate`/`possibleDuplicateOf`, and the relevant class javadocs.\n\n**Tests**: `./mvnw -o test` \u2192 `Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `coreIdentityKeyIsSha256Hex` (64-hex shape) and `coreRejectsDuplicateIdentity` (409 on identical identity) both pass; **BUILD SUCCESS**.",
